# Slice 296 (ABSENT-HEAD-WRITE-NORM; the book provenance :468-476; the author 2026-10-05 and steps/free-names.md 2026-10-03;
# Codex, the 290 review, item 1): a head that no formal, no visible outer value and no established free input binds defines a
# named Structure with the content written after it -- a name as that content too -- in a method, at the unit's root, inside a
# named Structure and at a part's root (absent_head_definition_part.lm2).  `call:` executes such a Structure, so a primitive
# there would be refused.  On the tuple of 295 every such line with a name as its tail was refused at translation (`an
# unknown head needs a Structure body`, the fixture absent_head_name_refused of slice 290).  Entry 7; 81.. name the check.
int: j 3
x: j
T:
    int: a 1
    fld: a
end: T
sub: put_absent (int: v)
    absent_name: v
end: put_absent
fn: f () int
    int: i 3
    y: i
    call: y
    return: i + 4
end: f
int: code 7
call: x
if: j != 3
    code: 81
---
call: T\fld
if: code = 7 && T\a != 1
    code: 82
---
put_absent(1)
